            "heading_ft6Xne": {
              "type": "heading",
              "name": "Heading",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "It wasn't laziness. It was anxiety. (We know now.)",
                "heading_type": "h2",
                "heading_size": "heading-h2"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "richtext_bRQ6qi": {
              "type": "richtext",
              "name": "Richtext",
              "settings": {
                "richtext": "<p>Awkward AF wasn't born in a boardroom. It was born from that very specific moment where you look back at your younger self and think: I wasn't lazy. I wasn't difficult. I was just really, really struggling.</p><p>For years, anxiety made the world feel heavier than it looked. Social situations that seemed simple to everyone else felt like navigating a minefield in flip-flops. Motivation wasn't missing, it was buried under a mountain of \"what if everything goes wrong.\" From the outside, it probably just looked like not trying very hard.</p><p>Turns out, that's a surprisingly relatable experience.</p>"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            }
          },
          "block_order": [
            "heading_ft6Xne",
            "richtext_bRQ6qi"
          ]
        }
      },
